    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d999">

                <pb facs="1050" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/3693</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the French Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Jusserand</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1694</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to the Department’s note
                    of December 29 last,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d999-f1"/> regarding the presence of
                    the French cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Descartes</hi> in the vicinity of San
                    Juan, and various incidents connected therewith, and your personal note of
                    December 30 last,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d999-f2"/> in which you stated that you
                    were making the necessary inquiries on the points mentioned in my <pb
                        facs="1051" n="765" xml:id="pg765"/> note, I have the honor to ask whether
                    you have received any replies to your inquiries.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
